    "8 MiB is a per-inode logical value budget, not deduplicated physical usage, reservation or repository quota. Count/byte rejections precede publication; shrinking/removal allows retry without reopening storage.",
    "Existing <=32-name, <=262143-byte-per-value inodes fit the new budget. Older daemons reject attribute lists/verification above 32 names.",
